WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:08.291
Telo Ride 1 is now static files: the app's build on a static host, and no backend.

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.584
The build carries its host's configuration, in one file: the way back to the app for

00:00:15.584 --> 00:00:20.205
its routes, the security headers, a year of HSTS and the cache rules.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:28.521
So the class ride opens by its own address, and an unknown address reaches page not

00:00:28.521 --> 00:00:32.648
found. A file that is not there is not found, never the app.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:41.640
The host is Azure Static Web Apps. It redirects plain http itself, so a person

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.246
checks that on the real host. No test may leave this machine.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:54.404
The backend is gone, whole: four projects, fifteen migrations and thirty-two tests.

00:00:54.404 --> 00:00:57.548
Verify and the pipeline check the app alone.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.035
The class fits a phone, a tablet and a desktop, as it did before.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.669
Seven specs came first, and all seven failed. Now one hundred and seventy-nine specs

00:01:17.669 --> 00:01:19.577
and every unit test pass.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:30.825
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:30.825 --> 00:01:32.021
nothing else.

00:01:32.366 --> 00:01:37.318
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:37.318 --> 00:01:42.330
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:45.831
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:46.176 --> 00:01:50.152
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
